{
 "title": "Why the Pythagorean Theorem Works",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "The Right Triangle",
   "say": "Let's start with any right-angled triangle having legs a and b, and hypotenuse c.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "Why Does a² + b² = c² Work?",
     "size": 52,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri_demo",
     "d": "M 150 350 L 350 350 L 150 200 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "rt_angle",
     "x": 150,
     "y": 330,
     "w": 20,
     "h": 20,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_a",
     "x": 115,
     "y": 265,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_b",
     "x": 240,
     "y": 365,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_c",
     "x": 260,
     "y": 250,
     "text": "c",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Arrange Four Triangles",
   "say": "Now place four identical copies of this triangle inside a large square of side length a + b.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "outer_sq",
     "x": 600,
     "y": 180,
     "w": 400,
     "h": 400,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri_1",
     "d": "M 600 300 L 720 180 L 600 180 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri_2",
     "d": "M 720 180 L 1000 300 L 1000 180 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri_3",
     "d": "M 1000 300 L 880 580 L 1000 580 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri_4",
     "d": "M 880 580 L 600 460 L 600 580 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_out_top_a",
     "x": 650,
     "y": 135,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_out_top_b",
     "x": 850,
     "y": 135,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Inspect the Inner Tilt",
   "say": "Notice the tilted square formed in the center: each side has length c.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "inner_sq",
     "d": "M 600 300 L 720 180 L 1000 300 L 880 580 Z",
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5,
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_inner_c",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 360,
     "text": "Area = c²",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Calculate Total Area",
   "say": "The big square's area is (a + b)², which also equals the four blue triangles plus the center square c².",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_line1",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 220,
     "text": "Total Area of Big Square:",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_line2",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 270,
     "text": "(a + b)²",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_line3",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 340,
     "text": "= 4 · (½ · a · b) + c²",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_line4",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 410,
     "text": "= 2ab + c²",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Expand and Simplify",
   "say": "Expand the left side to get a² + 2ab + b². Subtract 2ab from both sides, and a² + b² = c² remains!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_expand",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 480,
     "text": "a² + 2ab + b² = 2ab + c²",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "strike_left",
     "x1": 1165,
     "y1": 505,
     "x2": 1245,
     "y2": 505,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "strike_right",
     "x1": 1345,
     "y1": 505,
     "x2": 1425,
     "y2": 505,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "box_result",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 550,
     "w": 380,
     "h": 90,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "final_pythagoras",
     "x": 1290,
     "y": 575,
     "text": "a² + b² = c²",
     "size": 44,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Geometric Meaning",
   "say": "So the sum of the areas of squares on the two legs always equals the area of the square on the hypotenuse.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "summary_note",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 720,
     "text": "Area of Square(a) + Area of Square(b) = Area of Square(c)",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "qed_note",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 790,
     "text": "This geometric harmony holds for every right triangle!",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "gray",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}